      "id": "lj2sztv",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Background: Rise of New Religions"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Vardhamana Mahavira propagated Jainism as the 24th Tirthankara, emphasizing strict non-violence (Ahimsa).",
        "Jainism prescribes the Triratna (Three Jewels) comprising Right Faith, Right Knowledge, and Right Conduct.",
        "Gautama Buddha founded Buddhism and taught the Four Noble Truths to end human suffering.",
        "Buddhism advocates the Eightfold Path (Ashtangika Marga) as a Middle Path between extreme asceticism and indulgence.",
        "Four major Buddhist Councils were held to preserve Buddhist teachings, eventually leading to sects like Hinayana and Mahayana."
      ],
      "id": "xevv8vu"
    },
